  "category": "questions",
  "explanation": {
    "en": "どこ means “where.” It is used to ask about location. You can use it with particles like に, で, and へ depending on the meaning.\n\nKey points:\n• どこに = where (location/existence)\n• どこで = where (action place)\n• どこへ = where (destination)\n• Common in daily questions\n\nExample: “トイレはどこですか” means “Where is the toilet?” “どこで勉強しますか” means “Where do you study?”\n\nUse に with existence or location, で with actions, and へ with destinations. This is a great way to practice particles too.\n\nPractice by asking about places: どこに住んでいますか, どこで働きますか.",
    "ja": ""
  },
